-------------
Polymorphism is a fundamental concept in object-oriented programming (OOP) that allows a single entity, such as a method or object, to take on multiple forms. In Java, polymorphism enables methods 
or objects to behave differently based on their context, particularly at runtime.
Polymorphism in Java allows the same method to behave differently based on the object at runtime (overriding) or based on parameters at compile time (overloading)

